# Contributing

## Setup

```bash
git clone {{ repo_url }}.git
cd {{ repo_name }}
uv sync --all-groups
uv run pre-commit install --install-hooks
```

## Branching and pull requests

`main` is never committed to directly. Every change gets its own branch and a
pull request.

Branch names are `<type>/<short-slug>`, kebab-case, where `<type>` is a
Conventional Commits type (`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`,
`ci`, `build`) — pick the type the branch's eventual squash commit will carry,
e.g. `fix/retry-timeout` or `docs/update-readme`.

```bash
git switch -c <type>/<short-slug>
# ... commit(s) ...
git push -u origin <type>/<short-slug>
```

Open a pull request and wait for CI to pass, then **squash merge**: it keeps
one commit per change on `main`, and the squash commit's subject is what
`git log` shows afterwards, so edit it into a proper Conventional Commits
subject rather than leaving GitHub's default title.

## Before opening a pull request

```bash
uv run poe check
```

Runs formatting, lint, type checking, and tests — the same gate CI runs.

## Commit messages

Commits follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)
(`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, ...); a `commit-msg` hook enforces this.
{%- if changelog_tool == 'git-cliff' %} `CHANGELOG.md` is generated from
this history, so write messages for a reader who was not in the pull
request.
{%- endif %}

## Keeping up with the template

This project was scaffolded from a Copier template and can pull in later
template changes:

```bash
uvx copier update --trust
```

Review the three-way merge carefully. `copier update` compares your working
tree against the template's old and new versions of each file — local edits
in the middle of a templated file merge cleanly, but **edits appended at the
very end of a file can be lost**: both the template and your change add
content at the same place with no trailing context for the merge to anchor
to, and the incoming template version wins. If you need to add something
project-specific to the end of a templated file, prefer inserting it above
any stable trailing section (e.g. above the License heading) rather than
appending after it.

Never delete or hand-edit `.copier-answers.yml` — `copier update` needs it to
know what was asked and answered.
